# ============================================================
# AGS WEBWORKS — environment variables (EXAMPLE — safe to commit)
# Copy to .env (local) or set in Vercel → Settings → Environment
# Variables. NEVER commit the real .env file.
# ============================================================

# ---------- DATABASE (required) ----------
# PostgreSQL connection string. Two ways to run:
#
# 1) Supabase (recommended — what the Vercel guide uses):
#    - For the VERCEL RUNTIME use the "Transaction pooler" string (port 6543):
#      postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1
#    - For ONE-OFF COMMANDS from your machine (db:push / db:seed) use the
#      "Direct connection" string (port 5432):
#      postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
#
# 2) Local development without any service: leave DATABASE_URL unset (or a
#    file: URL) — an embedded PostgreSQL starts automatically via
#    `bun run dev` / `bun run db:setup`. Nothing to configure.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abcdefghijk:your-password@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1

# ---------- SCHEDULER (recommended in production) ----------
# Shared secret for the recurring-invoice scheduler endpoint
# (/api/maintenance/scheduler/run). Also set as CRON_SECRET in Vercel so the
# built-in Vercel Cron job is authorized. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# SCHEDULER_KEY=some-long-random-string

# ---------- EMERGENCY ACCESS (owner only — optional) ----------
# If set, this single password can sign in to ANY active account even after
# personal password changes (owner "break-glass" access; never shown in the
# UI; every use is recorded in the activity log). Keep it long and private.
# DISABLE IT (leave unset) before handing the system to a client.
# EMERGENCY_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-private-password
